#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:92
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You can always change the tick rate as you develop, it is as simple as "
"changing the project setting."
msgstr "你可以在开发过程中随时更改 tick 速率，只需修改项目设置即可。"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:96
msgid "Call ``reset_physics_interpolation()`` when teleporting objects"
msgstr "传送对象时调用 ``reset_physics_interpolation()``"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:98
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Most of the time, interpolation is what you want between two physics ticks. "
"However, there is one situation in which it may *not* be what you want. That "
"is when you are initially placing objects, or moving them to a new location. "
"Here, you don't want a smooth motion between where the object was (e.g. the "
"origin) and the initial position - you want an instantaneous move."
msgstr ""
"大多数情况下，在两次物理帧之间进行插值是你想要的效果。然而，有一种情况可能*不"
"*适合使用插值。那就是当你最初放置物体，或者将物体移动到新位置时。在这种情况"
"下，你并不希望在物体原来的位置（例如原点）和初始位置之间进行平滑移动——你想要"
"的是瞬间移动。"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:104
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The solution to this is to call "
"the :ref:`Node.reset_physics_interpolation<class_Node_method_reset_physics_interpolation>` "
"function. What this function does under the hood is set the internally "
"stored *previous transform* of the object to be equal to the *current "
"transform*. This ensures that when interpolating between these two equal "
"transforms, there will be no movement."
msgstr ""
"解决这个问题的方法是调"
"用 :ref:`Node.reset_physics_interpolation<class_Node_method_reset_physics_interpolation>` "
"函数。这个函数在底层的作用是将对象内部存储的*上一帧变换*设置为与*当前变换*相"
"等。这确保了在这两个相等的变换之间进行插值时，不会产生任何移动。"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:110
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Even if you forget to call this, it will usually not be a problem in most "
"situations (especially at high tick rates). This is something you can easily "
"leave to the polishing phase of your game. The worst that will happen is "
"seeing a streaking motion for a frame or so when you move them - you will "
"know when you need it!"
msgstr ""
"即使你忘记调用这个方法，在大多数情况下通常也不会出现问题（尤其是在高帧率"
"下）。你可以很容易地将这个问题留到游戏打磨阶段再处理。最坏的情况就是在移动它"
"们时可能会看到一帧左右的拖影效果——当你需要时自然会知道！"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:116
msgid "There are actually two ways to use ``reset_physics_interpolation()``:"
msgstr "实际上有两种使用 ``reset_physics_interpolation()`` 的方法："

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:118
msgid "*Standing start (e.g. player)*"
msgstr "*立定起步（例如玩家）*"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:120
#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:128
msgid "Set the initial transform"
msgstr "设置初始变换"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:121
#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:129
msgid "Call ``reset_physics_interpolation()``"
msgstr "调用 ``reset_physics_interpolation()``"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:123
msgid ""
"The previous and current transforms will be identical, resulting in no "
"initial movement."
msgstr "上一个变换和当前变换相同，因此不会产生初始移动。"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:126
msgid "*Moving start (e.g. bullet)*"
msgstr "*移动起步（例如子弹）*"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:130
msgid "Immediately set the transform expected after the first tick of motion"
msgstr "第一个运动周期后会立即设置变换"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:132
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The previous transform will be the starting position, and the current "
"transform will act as though a tick of simulation has already taken place. "
"This will immediately start moving the object, instead of having a tick "
"delay standing still."
msgstr ""
"前一个变换将作为起始位置，当前变换将表现得好像已经进行了一次模拟 tick。这将立"
"即开始移动对象，而不是有一个 tick 的延迟静止不动。"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:136
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Make sure you set the transform and call ``reset_physics_interpolation()`` "
"in the correct order as shown above, otherwise you will see unwanted "
"\"streaking\"."
msgstr ""
"请确保你按照上面所示的正确顺序设置变换并调用 "
"``reset_physics_interpolation()``，否则你可能会看到不希望的\"拖影\"现象。"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:141
msgid "Testing and debugging tips"
msgstr "测试和调试贴士"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:143
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Even if you intend to run physics at 60 TPS, in order to thoroughly test "
"your interpolation and get the smoothest gameplay, it is highly recommended "
"to temporarily set the physics tick rate to a low value such as 10 TPS."
msgstr ""
"即使你打算以 60 TPS 的物理帧率运行游戏，为了彻底测试你的插值并实现最流畅的游"
"戏体验，强烈建议暂时将物理帧率设置为较低的值，例如 10 TPS。"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:147
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The gameplay may not work perfectly, but it should enable you to more easily "
"see cases where you should be "
"calling :ref:`Node.reset_physics_interpolation<class_Node_method_reset_physics_interpolation>`, "
"or where you should be using your own custom interpolation on e.g. "
"a :ref:`Camera3D<class_Camera3D>`. Once you have these cases fixed, you can "
"set the physics tick rate back to the desired setting."
msgstr ""
"游戏玩法可能无法完美运行，但它应该能让你更容易看到在哪些情况下应该调"
"用 :ref:`Node.reset_physics_interpolation<class_Node_method_reset_physics_interpolation>`，"
"或者在哪些情况下你应该在例如 :ref:`Camera3D<class_Camera3D>` 上使用自己的自定"
"义插值。一旦你修复了这些情况，就可以将物理 tick 速率设置回所需的值。"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:153
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The other great advantage to testing at a low tick rate is you can often "
"notice other game systems that are synchronized to the physics tick and "
"creating glitches which you may want to work around. Typical examples "
"include setting animation blend values, which you may decide to set in "
"``_process()`` and interpolate manually."
msgstr ""
"以较低 tick 速率进行测试的另一个巨大优势是，你通常可以注意到其他与物理 tick "
"同步的游戏系统，并发现可能想要解决的故障。典型的例子包括设置动画混合值，你可"
"能会决定在 ``_process()`` 中设置并手动进行插值。"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:160
msgid ""
"In 2D, the position of visible collision shapes shown by the :menu:`Debug > "
"Visible Collision Shapes` option **will** take physics interpolation into "
"account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:164
msgid ""
"By contrast, in 3D, the position of visible collision shapes **will not** "
"take physics interpolation into account. This means the visible collision "
"shapes can appear to move less smoothly and appear slightly in front of the "
"object's visual representation when the object is moving. This is not a bug, "
"but a consequence of how physics interpolation is implemented in 3D."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:4
msgid "Advanced physics interpolation"
msgstr "高级物理插值"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:6
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Although the previous instructions will give satisfactory results in a lot "
"of games, in some cases you will want to go a stage further to get the best "
"possible results and the smoothest possible experience."
msgstr ""
"虽然前面的说明在很多游戏中都能给出令人满意的结果，但在某些情况下，你可能需要"
